 "plan": {
  "artifact": "astra-46-2b-source-map-v7-plan",
  "purpose": "Bounded, read-only recheck of the five employers source map v6 left UNRESOLVED, plus PureHealth, whose v6 MANUAL_LINK was obtained after its robots.txt answered with a Cloudflare 403, which the v4 rule treats as 'do not fetch this host'. Run once with scripts/source_route_check.py from the Owner's machine. No ATS tenant is requested on branding alone, no job-listing API is called, no form is submitted and no e-mail is sent.",
  "notes": [
   "DNS steps only resolve conventional careers hostnames on the employer's own registered domain; they contact no host. A resolving name is followed up only in a separate, recorded plan.",
   "HCT: only the www origin is requested. Its robots.txt redirects to the apex host, so one check covers both hosts without repeating the six-contact loop.",
   "ZU: the presented certificate is not read, because the TLS connection is reset before a certificate is presented.",
   "PureHealth: one robots check under the restored v4 rule. Only if robots.txt is readable and allows it is the homepage requested, to see whether it still links 'Careers' to a jobs route."
  ],
